<!-- Handoff industries/banking-financial-services.html: misses. Native Astro markup; shared document shell is V9Layout. -->
<section class="g-white" id="misses">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow"><span class="tick">\</span> 02 · Where a generic screen breaks</div>
    <h2 style="--d:60ms">Four things a CV can’t tell you.</h2>
    <p class="lead" style="--d:120ms">
      None of them are exotic. They’re invisible to anyone assessing from outside the sector, which is most of the
      people doing the assessing.
    </p>
    <ol class="ix-miss">
      <li style="--d:0ms">
        <span class="ab-k">01</span><div>
          <h3>Compliance instinct</h3><span class="ix-lbl">Invisible on paper</span>
        </div><div>
          <p>
            Risk appetite and audit mindset can’t be read off a job title. Someone who has never had a control fail on
            their watch interviews the same as someone who has.
          </p><p class="ix-tell">
            <span>Where it shows up</span>the incident they were closest to, and what changed afterwards.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li><li style="--d:70ms">
        <span class="ab-k">02</span><div>
          <h3>Domain depth in engineers</h3><span class="ix-lbl">A generic tech screen misses it</span>
        </div><div>
          <p>
            Core banking integrations, payment rails, data residency. An excellent backend engineer with none of it will
            clear a standard interview comfortably.
          </p><p class="ix-tell">
            <span>Where it shows up</span>what they had to hold still while everything else moved.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li><li style="--d:140ms">
        <span class="ab-k">03</span><div>
          <h3>Seniority that means something</h3><span class="ix-lbl">AVP and VP travel badly</span>
        </div><div>
          <p>
            Titles vary between institutions. A VP at one bank runs a function. At another, they run a spreadsheet. The
            CV can’t tell you which.
          </p><p class="ix-tell"><span>Where it shows up</span>what they were accountable for when it went wrong.</p>
        </div>
      </li><li style="--d:210ms">
        <span class="ab-k">04</span><div>
          <h3>Speed, because they have offers</h3><span class="ix-lbl">Slow pipelines lose the good ones</span>
        </div><div>
          <p>Strong BFSI candidates hold two or three offers at once. A four-week process loses them.</p><p
            class="ix-tell"
          >
            <span>Where it shows up</span>three scored names in about 36 hours, so the clock is yours.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>
